AssetRateLimits
├── given an unconfigured or disabled asset
│   └── it rejects consumption and exposes zero capacity
├── when configuring a zero duration
│   └── it reverts without changing state
├── given an active period
│   ├── when changing the maximum or disabling and reenabling
│   │   └── it preserves spent assets and the period boundary
│   ├── when changing the duration
│   │   └── it carries spent assets into a period starting now
│   └── when cumulative spending exceeds the cap
│       └── it reverts without overflow or state changes
├── given an expired period
│   ├── it resets usage at the exact boundary
│   ├── it does not accumulate unused capacity
│   └── it keeps fixed boundaries after long idle times
└── given a sequence of spending and time jumps
    └── it never exceeds each period's cumulative cap
